--- !u!114 &1283812438662089816
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9846b17575a458d45aec9532bc18d459, type: 3}
  m_Name: Note
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  position: {x: 1193.19, y: -208.6}
  dynamicConnectionPorts: []
  backgroundColor: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  extraSize: {x: 100, y: 300}
  text: "If talked to before this stage is complete:\r\nAmrita: Get a fruitant to
    follow you with a sweet ingredient, then lead it back here.\r\nAmrita: Yes, you
    can charm a Paddle Pear with its own pear.\r\nAmrita: No, you shouldn\u2019t think
    about it too hard. \r\n\r\nSpicy Tutorial:\r\n\r\nAmrita (happy): Excellent. Now,
    these ingredients have uses in combat as well. \r\nAmrita: Horseradishes are common
    here, and will gift you a spicy radish.\r\nAmrita: If a fruitant eats something
    spicy, it\u2019ll start to breathe fireballs.\r\nAmrita: Don\u2019t ask me how;
    I\u2019m not a biologist. \r\nAmrita: As an aside, this might be combined with
    sweets for some mobile protection.\r\nAmrita: Anyway, use this fire effect to
    destroy some nearby foliage and we\u2019ll be done.\r\nAmrita (happy): Heh. You\u2019d
    also be doing me a favor by clearing more space for our camp.\n"
